            "notes": "Option 2: I\u2019m an Average Player\n\nThis build is for those games where you want the raw healing power, and just a little bit of that additional security. This offers a lot of healing, but less survivability. You are more reliant on positioning and ensuring that you never leave your safety with Caduceus Ex, but that\u2019s okay, because that\u2019s all you really need.\n\n![Image](https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/606007873880719382/1405810952800178197/image.png?ex=68a02ef9&is=689edd79&hm=96e7647b974e67991559a0c52fae604db56f1fcf7343c37d1fe6ad2db712fb1f&=&format=webp&quality=lossless \"large\")\n\nCore Build\n\nAmari\u2019s Antidote - The lifesaver and core of your build. Get it.\n\nBooster Jets - The best Attack Speed Item you can buy. Get it.\n\nEye of the Spider - A big stat stick. Get it.\n\nChain Evoker - Helps with survivability and buffs blue beam. A Mercy must-have.\n\nHardlight Accelerator - Adds a new multiplier to your healing. (70 HPS) Get it.\n\nAverage Comfy Items\n\nCaduceus Ex - Helps you heal people from farther away without abandoning cover. This helps with tanks and flankers who love to dive the enemy team and you will die if you follow.",
